\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Multiplying the transverse directions}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On a momentum axis the Hermitian symbol from \ref{fdip-009Q}
is a scalar times one direction operator. A turn in a transverse
plane instead contains a product of two directions. In dimension
three, multiplying that product by the axial direction uses
every axis once. What information does the full ordered product
supply about the turn?}
